<title>BELGIUM: Belgian tax receipts up 4.0% in nine mths to Sept.</title>
<headline>Belgian tax receipts up 4.0% in nine mths to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Belgian fiscal receipts were up 4.2 percent in September from September 1995 and up 4.0 percent in the first nine months of 1996 from the same 1995 period, the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Monday.  </p>
<p>    TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr) Sep 96	 Sep 95    pct change</p>
<p>    Total			   142,536	136,855	4.2</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		79,513	 71,429     11.3</p>
<p>	Non-div. witholding tax   5,222	  6,830    -23.5</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes    37,950	 39,904     -4.9</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>					Jan-Sep 96   Jan-Sep 95 pct change</p>
<p>    Total			   1,642,197    1,578,526    4.0</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		 957,554	926,434    3.4</p>
<p>	Non-div. withholding tax   53,373	 64,614  -17.4</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes     429,236	413,532    3.8</p>
<p>The statement said that the fall in receipts from withholding tax on fixed income investments (not including dividends from shares) was due to the fall in interest rates and to an increase in withholding tax.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
